# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Without this, git converts to CRLF on Windows, and two kinds of check break
# there for reasons that have nothing to do with the code: the generated-file
# tests compare `make docs` output (always LF) against a checked-out file
# (CRLF), and the release-config scan looks for "\n    goos:" anchors that CRLF
# splits apart. Both reported real-looking failures — "docs/clients.md does not
# match the adapters", ".goreleaser.yaml has no goos list" — that were purely
# line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fixtures whose bytes are the point. A conformance case exists to be loaded
# exactly as written, and the corpus digest covers its contents.
conformance/cases/** -text
internal/*/testdata/** -text
internal/*/*/testdata/** -text

# Binary.
*.png binary
